9907 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9da6b88c-3427-5d82-9c0a-0c12e0c3ee52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186569811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186569711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569912 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a8483fff-76a3-580a-a83e-5302b7c416d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569957 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569957 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334280" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569957 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569957 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569957 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "047ba9d9-f028-5122-88f6-0f2794537abb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569957 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental matrix could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569972 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569972 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334287" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569972 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569972 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569972 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2812ec6f-62e9-58a6-b999-e2e9bb1ef20a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569972 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{t} \\\\ -{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 3{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{t} & {e}^{5t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & 3{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570004 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570004 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570004 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570004 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570004 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "808ef5db-aeee-5e2b-ba0b-cf24a0046d0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570004 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}=\\begin{bmatrix}(t+2){e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & (t+2){e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570064 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570064 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6298b8c6-ac0a-5b25-bb40-7c5832588d35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570064 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186569957 #edb/ref 17592186045417